NAME
       http_fetch, http_request - HTTP client

SYNOPSIS
       #include <http.h>

       int http_fetch(const char *url, ...);
       int http_request(...);
       int http_jar_set(...);
       int http_jar_header(...);

DESCRIPTION
       Performs an HTTP or HTTPS request and returns the status, the
       headers and the body. HTTPS goes through the TLS client, so the
       certificate chain is verified unless verification is turned off.

       Redirects are followed up to a caller-supplied limit, and a
       small cookie jar carries Set-Cookie values into later requests
       on the same host.

       This is the code behind wget and curl.

RETURN VALUE
       The HTTP status on success, negative on a transport or TLS
       failure.

SEE ALSO
       tls(3), x509(3), wget(1), curl(1)
